  Copyright (c) 2025 xesf.  Licensed under the MIT licence; the full text is
  in third_party/h264dec/LICENSE.

Local changes (all documented in third_party/h264dec/README.md): intra
prediction falls back to DC when a corrupt stream selects a mode whose
neighbour is outside the picture, and a few shifts of negative values were
rewritten as multiplications so the code is clean under UBSan.  Neither
change affects the decoded output.

The H.264 decode path (include/video_decoder_backend.h,
src/h264_video_decoder.cpp) and the in-memory deinterlacer
(src/deinterlace.cpp) replace libavcodec, libswscale and libavfilter: the
default build links no FFmpeg library at all.


2b. FFmpeg — LGPL-2.1-or-later (optional A/B build only)
--------------------------------------------------------
Setting `-DUMDPLAY_NATIVE_VIDEO=OFF` or `-DUMDPLAY_NATIVE_ATRAC3P=OFF` builds
the optional libav* decoder backends (src/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cpp,
src/ffmpeg_audio_decoder.cpp), which link the system libavcodec/libavutil (and
libswresample for audio).  Those libraries are not part of this source tree and
are never used by a default build.


